-- title:
--   Gauss valuations of X₀(Mp) are inert in X(Γ₁(M)∩Γ₀(p))
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_1$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ (with nonzero denominator), and let $K_2$ be the analogous field for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$; let $\iota_2 \colon K_2 \to K_1$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the two inclusions into $L((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K_1$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K_1$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNumQ}$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$ containing the image of $A$, sending the maximal ideal of $A$ into the nonunits of $V$, and such that for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ with nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$. Let $V_2$ be the valuation subring of $K_2$ defined by $y \in V_2 \iff \iota_2 y \in V$, with algebra maps $V_2 \to V$ and $\kappa(V_2) \to \kappa(V)$ compatible with $\iota_2$ and with the residue maps. Then $[\kappa(V) : \kappa(V_2)] = \mathrm{relfinrank}\,K_2\,K_1$, and $\kappa(V)/\kappa(V_2)$ is separable.
--
--   This is the inertness statement for the Gauss (branch) valuations in the extension of $q$-expansion function fields attached to $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)) \to X_0(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$ containing $\zeta_p$: the residue extension realises the whole relative degree and is separable, so the corresponding place is inert with trivial ramification and a single place above. It feeds the bounds on inertia groups and the unramifiedness assertions at stalks of the two-chart integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneGammaZeroP_finrank_residueField_valuationSubring_eq_finrank_and_isSeparable_of_gauss_x1x0_gamma0.lean

